{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"amoeboid-amateur-guillemot","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe mechanism ratchet has two contracts that disagree about markers. The gate and the unit tests honour them: `evaluate()` (`scripts/_mechanism_delta/compare.py:89-101`) partitions new and increased keys into admitted and unadmitted by exact-key `# mechanism-ok:` marker, and `tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py:357-364` asserts `set(baseline) | admitted == live`, so a marker-admitted mechanism is deliberately absent from `.github/mechanism-baseline.json`. The drain does not: `_run_update_stale` (`scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py:177-195`) computes `compare(current, baseline)` (`compare.py:45-57`, marker-blind) and refuses whenever `counters.has_regression` is true (`compare.py:34-35`). Consequences on origin/main 083620b0: (1) a change that removes a censused mechanism and, in the same tree, adds a marker-admitted one cannot drain the removed row, so `test_the_committed_baseline_matches_the_live_tree` fails on the stale row and the only way through is the forbidden hand-edit (the wall the agent on Gerrit change 2658 hit, recorded on celadon-computable-smelts a1f1-a30d-2d50-4f5a); (2) once any marker-admitted mechanism is in the tree without a baseline row, every later `--update-stale` refuses for everyone until an administrator edits the file. The config-cleanup story citified-earth-cottontail (b939-bc68-1cb2-4ee9) removes two env-var reads and adds a marked `tests/_child_hooks.py` helper in one change, so it is blocked by this defect; nine other breaking-release stories drain removed mechanisms and would be blocked the moment that helper lands. Operator decision 2026-09-07: the drain in the same change is the sanctioned step for removals, and the marker remains the sanctioned path for additions, so the drain must honour markers exactly as the gate does.\n\n## Approach\nMake the drain's refusal the gate's own verdict. In `_run_update_stale`, replace the `compare()` plus `has_regression` refusal with `code, lines = evaluate(current, baseline, markers_for(repo_root))` and refuse (print the report lines to stderr, return 1, baseline byte-identical) when `code != 0`; otherwise `drain_stale(current, baseline)` and write as today. `drain_stale` only drops keys, so admitted keys stay out of the baseline and the unit-test invariant `set(baseline) | admitted == live` continues to describe the written file. A blank marker still refuses through `evaluate`'s blank-marker errors. Reword the two prose statements of the old rule: `docs/architecture.md:674-677` becomes \"`--update-stale` drops entries whose definition site is gone and rewrites canonical sorted JSON. It refuses to write, leaving the baseline byte-identical, while any UNADMITTED mechanism is new or increased, so it can never bless a regression; a marker-admitted mechanism does not block it. Run it in the same change whenever your change removes a mechanism and `--check` reports only stale rows; a contributor never hand-edits the baseline.\" `AGENTS.md:389-390` becomes \"Do not hand-edit `.github/mechanism-baseline.json`. When your own change removes a mechanism, run `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --update-stale` in that change and commit the shrunken baseline; the drain refuses while any unadmitted mechanism is new or increased, so it cannot bless a regression.\" Extend the source-level pin at `tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py` (about `:480-530`, the test that asserts the two committed-tree tests consult `markers_for`) to also cover `_run_update_stale`, so a wholesale revert cannot silently make the drain marker-blind again (the failure mode recorded on satin-fullgrown-shibainu affd-913c-3fb0-40fb).\n\n## Scope\n`scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py` (`_run_update_stale`, the `--update-stale` help text at the parser), `docs/architecture.md` (the drain paragraph), `AGENTS.md` (the mechanism-ratchet paragraph), `tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py`. Out of scope: `compare()` and `evaluate()` themselves, the detectors, the complexity ratchet, `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` (unchanged by this fix; `--check` on the committed tree reports `new=0`).\n\n## Testing\nRed first: new `test_update_stale_drains_while_an_admitted_mechanism_stands` in `tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py`, built like `test_update_stale_refuses_to_write_while_a_regression_stands` (`:338-350`): baseline `{\"lock::a.lock\": 1, \"lock::gone.lock\": 1}`, live `{\"a.lock\", \"marked.lock\"}` with a well-placed non-blank marker for `lock::marked.lock`; assert `main([\"--update-stale\"])` returns 0, the written baseline is exactly `{\"lock::a.lock\": 1}` (stale row dropped, admitted key not added), and a second run is a no-op. The existing refusal test stays green unchanged (an unmarked `surprise.lock` still refuses, baseline byte-identical). A second new test: a marker whose reason is blank still refuses. The pin test asserts `_run_update_stale`'s AST references `markers_for`. Then `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` and `--update-stale` on the committed tree (expected: `new=0`, no write), `make lint`, `make verify`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `--update-stale` writes when the only new or increased mechanisms are marker-admitted, drops the stale rows, and does not add the admitted keys; verified by the new unit test.\n- [ ] `--update-stale` still refuses, baseline byte-identical, on an unadmitted new mechanism and on a blank marker; verified by the existing refusal test plus the new blank-marker test.\n- [ ] The source-level pin covers `_run_update_stale`; verified by the extended pin test failing when the `markers_for` call is removed (recorded red-then-green in the commit message).\n- [ ] `docs/architecture.md` and `AGENTS.md` state the new rule and no longer say `--update-stale` is maintenance-only; verified by `grep -n \"maintenance-only\" AGENTS.md docs/architecture.md` returning only the complexity-ratchet `--lock` sentence.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0 and the committed baseline is unchanged (`git diff --exit-code .github/mechanism-baseline.json`).","id":"1768-5b6f-958a-43e9","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4","ratchet","ci","tooling"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"`check_mechanism_delta.py --update-stale` refuses on marker-admitted mechanisms, so a change that removes one mechanism and adds a justified one cannot pass the baseline test"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788809923346794596,"uuid":"7fcc2ca5-281b-49b1-bcf2-b958d578e25d"}